  "body": "Is it currently possible to create a fault-tolerant cluster of Synapse servers, where two or more Synapse servers look to the one PostgreSQL database?\r\nAs far as I can see, this is not possible now, because of stream_id generators (synapse/synapse/storage/util/id_generators.py), which are ok for one server but can have duplicate values in case of two or more servers.\r\nI think the correct solution should use PSQL sequences for stream_id generation (I'm trying to implement it right now). What do you think?",
